## 2026-08-05 — WiFi failsafe: auto-reboot if no link in 10s (post-milestone follow-up)
- wifi_manager: WIFI_CONNECTING now times out via WIFI_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS (10s) → handleConnectTimeout() → ESP.restart(). Success resets the counter.
- Reboot loop capped: wifiBootFailures (RTC_DATA_ATTR, survives restart, resets on power-cycle) — after WIFI_MAX_BOOT_FAILURES (3) consecutive failed boots, falls back to AP mode so the device stays configurable. startAPMode() clears the counter.
- connectToWiFi() resets connectStart; timeout checked before the retry branch so reboot wins cleanly. Runtime reconnects also reboot after 10s (energy persisted to NVS every 5s, max 5s loss).
- Build: PASS (1,182,841 B flash / 112,168 B RAM).

## 2026-08-06 — Noise floor quadrature + LPF actually applied (power_calculator.cpp)
- Fix 1: noise floor cancellation changed from LINEAR (`rawRMS - noiseFloor`) to QUADRATURE
  (`sqrt(max(raw^2 - floor^2, 0))`) in computeAll(). Phantom current fully gated when raw < floor.
- Fix 2: `lpfAlpha` (previously loaded from NVS but dead code) is now applied as a per-sample
  EMA low-pass in collectSamples() — voltage filtered with lpfAlpha[0] (matched filter keeps
  cross-correlation real power phase-accurate), each current channel with its own lpfAlpha[ch].
  alpha = 1.0 (default) = bypass, so behavior unchanged until user tunes it.
- Auto-zero unaffected: noiseFloor forced to 0 → signalRMS = rawRMS; lpfAlpha forced to 1.0
  by .ino during auto-zero → samples unfiltered.
- Build: PASS — PlatformIO espressif32/arduino, 1,047,593 B flash / 111,368 B RAM, -Wall clean
  (build differs from arduino-cli numbers due to toolchain version). UI/JS untouched.

## 2026-08-06 — Auto-zero noise floor uses median (outlier-robust)
- .ino auto-zero block: plain mean of 20 batches → MEDIAN of 32 batches (selection sort).
- One glitch batch (EMI spike / load flick-on / mains dip) can no longer skew the floor.
- lpfAlpha still forced to 1.0 and noiseFloor to 0 during capture → each batch = raw RMS.
- Build: PASS — PlatformIO espressif32/arduino, 1,047,665 B flash / 111,368 B RAM, -Wall clean.
